 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 183,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Cord or root? Motor exam + the LOWEST sensory level",
   "lines": [
    "upper motor neuron (UMN), brain or cord: subtle bulk loss, tone ↑, hyperreflexia, upgoing toe",
    "lower motor neuron (LMN), root or nerve: wasting, tone ↓, reflexes ↓ or absent",
    "NO motor or sensory function below the level, incl. rectal tone + perianal sensation = COMPLETE",
    "corticospinal crosses at the medullary PYRAMIDS · light touch uses both sensory pathways",
    "cord: UMN signs + a SYNDROME · root: LMN signs, more isolated · cord ends ~L1/L2, then cauda equina"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_cord",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 192,
   "w": 668,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "CORD (myelopathy): UMN below the level",
   "lines": [
    "cervical → arms + legs · thoracic → both legs ± bowel, bladder",
    "incomplete: WHICH modalities are lost names the syndrome"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_root",
   "x": 753,
   "y": 192,
   "w": 328,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "ROOTS (radiculopathy): LMN pattern",
   "lines": [
    "cervical → one arm · lumbar → one leg",
    "but beware cauda equina"
   ]
  },
